# Prepared acceptance cases only: no runner or step bindings exist before Gate A.
# Bind to real services/PostgreSQL and the shared browser harness after Gate A.
# Sources: docs/05-API-CONTRACT.md, docs/06-DOMAIN-RULES.md, docs/10-TEST-PLAN.md.
# Edge cases below reflect the coordinator-agreed planning contract; runtime bindings remain pending.
@pending_gate_a
Feature: Persisted, authorized subscription workflows
  Background:
    Given an isolated PostgreSQL test database and the injected Asia/Kolkata business date "2027-02-10"
    And an authenticated STAFF actor with valid mutation Origin and CSRF token

  @T10
  Scenario: Updating a template does not rewrite a quotation copied from it
    Given a template with plan "Monthly seats", validity 7 days, and 3 seats of product "Desk"
    And a subscription issued as QUOTATION from that template on "2027-02-09"
    When staff changes the template to another plan, validity 14 days, and 5 seats
    Then reloading the quotation preserves its copied plan, 3 seats, quoted prices and validity deadline

  @T11
  Scenario Outline: A subscription cannot skip a required lifecycle state
    Given a subscription in state "<state>"
    When staff requests action "<action>"
    Then the API returns 409 with error code INVALID_TRANSITION
    And no state, snapshot, period or invoice mutation is committed
    Examples:
      | state     | action   |
      | DRAFT     | confirm  |
      | DRAFT     | activate |
      | QUOTATION | activate |
      | ACTIVE    | confirm  |
      | CLOSED    | activate |

  @T11
  Scenario: An expired quote must be revised and reissued before confirmation
    Given a QUOTATION whose validity deadline was "2027-01-20"
    When staff requests confirm
    Then the API returns 409 with a useful quotation-expiry error
    And the subscription remains QUOTATION with unchanged snapshots
    When staff revises it, edits the draft and issues a new valid quotation
    Then staff can confirm that quotation and persist CONFIRMED

  @T11
  Scenario: Activation cannot precede the confirmed start date
    Given a CONFIRMED subscription starting "2027-02-11"
    When staff requests activate on "2027-02-10"
    Then the API returns 409 and the subscription remains CONFIRMED
    And no invoice is generated by the activation attempt

  @T10 @T11
  Scenario: Confirmation preserves quoted prices and freezes the agreed plan policies
    Given a valid QUOTATION issued with product unit price "1560.00" and allow_pause true
    When the catalog product price changes before staff confirms the quotation
    Then confirmation preserves the quoted unit price "1560.00"
    When the catalog plan disables pause after confirmation
    Then reloading the subscription retains allow_pause true in its confirmed plan snapshot

  @T12
  Scenario Outline: The backend enforces frozen plan policy switches
    Given an ACTIVE unexpired subscription with "<policy>" false in its confirmed plan snapshot
    And all already-due periods have durable outcomes
    When staff directly requests "<action>" regardless of the displayed action hints
    Then the API returns 409 with a useful policy error and no lifecycle mutation
    And reloaded UI communicates that the action is unavailable
    Examples:
      | policy            | action |
      | allow_pause       | pause  |
      | allow_early_close | close  |
      | allow_renew       | renew  |

  @T13
  Scenario: Pause and resume use original monthly boundaries without extending the term
    Given an ACTIVE monthly subscription anchored "2027-01-31" ending "2027-05-01" with allow_pause true
    And cycle 0 is INVOICED and next_cycle_index is 1
    When staff requests pause on "2027-02-10"
    Then state remains ACTIVE and an open pause starts "2027-02-28"
    And the existing invoice and billed period remain unchanged
    When billing runs as of "2027-02-28"
    Then cycle 1 has one durable PAUSED outcome, no invoice, and next_cycle_index is 2
    When staff requests resume on "2027-03-10"
    Then the pause ends "2027-03-31" and the subscription still ends "2027-05-01"
    When billing runs as of "2027-03-31"
    Then cycle 2 is billable once with period start "2027-03-31"

  @T13
  Scenario: A final shortened period retains the disclosed full-cycle price
    Given a valid QUOTATION for a monthly subscription anchored "2027-01-31" ending "2027-03-15"
    When staff reviews confirmation
    Then the screen explains no proration, no automatic refund, and the full-cycle charge
    When staff confirms, activates, and billing runs as of "2027-02-10"
    Then cycle 0 has a durable INVOICED outcome and next_cycle_index is 1
    When billing runs as of "2027-02-28" for the confirmed ACTIVE subscription
    Then the service period is "2027-02-28" through exclusive "2027-03-15"
    And billing uses one full-cycle price from the agreed snapshots
    And no period starts on or after "2027-03-15"

  @T13
  Scenario: Early close is scheduled rather than reported as immediate
    Given an ACTIVE monthly subscription anchored "2027-01-31" ending "2027-05-01" with allow_early_close true
    And cycle 0 is INVOICED and no already-due period is unprocessed
    When staff requests close on "2027-02-10"
    Then close_effective_on is "2027-02-28" and state remains ACTIVE
    And UI shows the scheduled closure date and retains the existing invoice
    When lifecycle processing runs on "2027-02-28"
    Then state becomes CLOSED and no period starts on or after "2027-02-28"

  @T13
  Scenario: Expiry without auto-close is visible and staff can finalize closure
    Given an ACTIVE subscription ending "2027-02-01" with auto_close false and allow_early_close false
    And every eligible period before expiry has a durable outcome
    When lifecycle processing runs on "2027-02-10"
    Then state remains ACTIVE with label "Expired, closure pending"
    And it is excluded from active-service counts and cannot start post-expiry periods
    When staff requests close
    Then state becomes CLOSED despite allow_early_close false

  @T12 @T13
  Scenario: Renewal creates a linked draft and does not reopen the old record
    Given an ACTIVE subscription ending "2027-05-01" with allow_renew true
    When staff renews with start "2027-05-01" and end "2027-08-01"
    Then a new unique reference is persisted in DRAFT with prior_subscription_id pointing to the original
    And the copied plan and lines belong to the new draft while the original remains unchanged
    And the new draft must pass quotation, confirmation and activation before billing

  @T12 @T13
  Scenario: Renewing a closed term leaves its terminal state unchanged
    Given a CLOSED subscription ending "2027-02-01" with allow_renew true
    When staff renews with start "2027-02-10" and end "2027-05-10"
    Then a new linked DRAFT with a new reference is created without back-billing the gap
    And the original remains CLOSED with its existing records unchanged

  @T12 @T13
  Scenario Outline: Renewal rejects overlap and backdated gaps
    Given a renewal-enabled original in state ACTIVE with effective end "<effective_end>"
    When staff renews with start "<new_start>" and end "2027-08-01"
    Then the request is rejected without creating a linked subscription
    Examples:
      | effective_end | new_start  |
      | 2027-05-01    | 2027-04-30 |
      | 2027-02-01    | 2027-02-09 |

  @T33
  Scenario Outline: Unprocessed due periods block repricing and schedule changes
    Given an ACTIVE monthly subscription anchored "2027-01-31" with next_cycle_index 0
    And policies permit pause and early close
    When staff requests "<action>" on "2027-02-10"
    Then the API returns 409 with error code DUE_BILLING_PENDING
    And lines, pause intervals, scheduled close, revision and existing financial records remain unchanged
    Examples:
      | action          |
      | change_quantity |
      | pause           |
      | close           |

  @T33
  Scenario: An unpaid invoice does not mean its cycle is unprocessed
    Given an ACTIVE monthly subscription anchored "2027-01-31" with cycle 0 INVOICED
    And its confirmed invoice is unpaid and next_cycle_index is 1
    When staff changes product quantity on "2027-02-10"
    Then the change is accepted for the next unprocessed cycle starting "2027-02-28"
    And the existing invoice snapshot remains unchanged and an audit event records the revision

  @T34
  Scenario: Lifecycle before billing does not strand a downtime backlog
    Given an ACTIVE daily subscription from "2027-02-01" through exclusive "2027-02-04" with auto_close true
    And no period outcomes exist after worker downtime
    When a worker tick processes lifecycle before billing with a billing batch limit of 1
    Then the subscription is not terminally closed while eligible periods remain without outcomes
    When subsequent worker ticks drain the backlog using the same ordering
    Then cycles 0, 1 and 2 each have one durable outcome before terminal closure
    And no period starts "2027-02-04" or later
    And retrying the worker creates no duplicate period or invoice

  @T06
  Scenario Outline: Customer A cannot access customer B's subscription
    Given authenticated CUSTOMER A and a subscription owned by CUSTOMER B
    When A requests "<method>" on B's portal subscription "<suffix>"
    Then the API returns 404 without revealing protected subscription details
    And no subscription, linked renewal or financial record is mutated
    Examples:
      | method | suffix  |
      | GET    | detail  |
      | POST   | pause   |
      | POST   | resume  |
      | POST   | close   |
      | POST   | renew   |

  @T06
  Scenario: The shared lifecycle service independently checks customer ownership
    Given CUSTOMER A's actor context and CUSTOMER B's pause-enabled ACTIVE subscription
    When apply_action is called for B's subscription as A with action pause
    Then ownership is rejected without mutation even without a portal route wrapper

  @R07
  Scenario Outline: Only product quantities satisfy the plan minimum
    Given an available plan with min_quantity 3 and one base-fee charge
    When staff creates a draft with total product quantity <quantity>
    Then the draft result is "<result>" without counting the base-fee charge as a product
    Examples:
      | quantity | result   |
      | 2        | rejected |
      | 3        | accepted |

  @R07
  Scenario: A clearly unavailable plan cannot be selected for an earlier service start
    Given a plan available from "2027-03-01"
    When staff creates a draft starting "2027-02-10"
    Then validation rejects the unavailable plan without persisting a subscription

  @T31
  Scenario: The real staff and customer journeys persist across reload
    Given real catalog data, a customer account and subscription-capable shared UI
    When staff creates a template and a draft, issues a quotation, confirms it and activates on its eligible date
    Then activation persists ACTIVE without issuing an invoice directly
    When the billing service runs due periods, confirms the invoice and records full payment
    And staff reloads the subscription detail and the customer reloads their own portal
    Then both show persisted permitted subscription details and the same paid invoice reference
    And every lifecycle action reflects its server result and effective date

  @T11
  Scenario Outline: Quotation validity is an exclusive business-date deadline
    Given an otherwise confirmable QUOTATION with quotation_valid_until "<deadline>"
    When staff requests confirm on the business date "2027-02-10"
    Then the confirmation outcome is "<outcome>"
    Examples:
      | deadline   | outcome                            |
      | 2027-02-09 | 409; state remains QUOTATION        |
      | 2027-02-10 | 409; state remains QUOTATION        |
      | 2027-02-11 | confirmed; state becomes CONFIRMED  |

  @R07
  Scenario Outline: Plan availability uses the requested service start in a half-open interval
    Given a plan available from "2027-02-10" until exclusive "2027-03-01"
    And an otherwise valid subscription request ending "2027-05-01"
    When staff creates the draft with requested start_date "<start_date>" on business date "2027-02-10"
    Then plan eligibility is "<result>" using start_date rather than today's date
    Examples:
      | start_date | result   |
      | 2027-02-09 | rejected |
      | 2027-02-10 | accepted |
      | 2027-02-28 | accepted |
      | 2027-03-01 | rejected |
      | 2027-03-02 | rejected |

  @T10 @R07
  Scenario Outline: SubscriptionCreate distinguishes omitted template lines from explicit overrides
    Given available plans P and Q each requiring minimum product quantity 3
    And template T selects plan P with lines "Desk:3"
    And all other SubscriptionCreate fields are valid
    When staff creates a subscription selecting template "<template>" and plan "<plan>" with lines "<lines>"
    Then draft creation is "<result>" and persisted lines are "<persisted_lines>"
    Examples:
      | template | plan | lines   | result   | persisted_lines |
      | T        | P    | omitted | accepted | Desk:3          |
      | T        | P    | Desk:4  | accepted | Desk:4          |
      | T        | P    | []      | rejected | no draft        |
      | T        | P    | null    | rejected | no draft        |
      | none     | P    | omitted | rejected | no draft        |
      | none     | P    | Desk:3  | accepted | Desk:3          |
      | T        | Q    | omitted | rejected | no draft        |

  @T11 @T33
  Scenario Outline: PATCH allows only fields appropriate to the current lifecycle state
    Given a subscription in state "<state>" from "2027-01-31" through exclusive "2027-05-01"
    And its due-period backlog is "<backlog>" and all other validation is satisfied
    When staff PATCHes the subscription with "<patch>" on business date "2027-02-10"
    Then the edit outcome is "<outcome>"
    And a rejected edit leaves dates, terms, lines, revision and existing invoice snapshots unchanged
    Examples:
      | state     | backlog | patch                       | outcome                         |
      | DRAFT     | none    | start_date=2027-02-11        | accepted                        |
      | DRAFT     | none    | end_date=2027-06-01          | accepted                        |
      | DRAFT     | none    | payment_terms_days=14        | accepted                        |
      | DRAFT     | none    | lines=Desk:4                | accepted                        |
      | QUOTATION | none    | start_date=2027-02-11        | rejected; revise to DRAFT first  |
      | QUOTATION | none    | payment_terms_days=14        | rejected; revise to DRAFT first  |
      | QUOTATION | none    | lines=Desk:4                | rejected; revise to DRAFT first  |
      | CONFIRMED | none    | start_date=2027-02-11        | rejected                        |
      | CONFIRMED | none    | payment_terms_days=14        | rejected                        |
      | CONFIRMED | none    | lines=Desk:4                | rejected                        |
      | CLOSED    | none    | start_date=2027-02-11        | rejected                        |
      | CLOSED    | none    | payment_terms_days=14        | rejected                        |
      | CLOSED    | none    | lines=Desk:4                | rejected                        |
      | ACTIVE    | none    | lines=Desk:4                | accepted for next cycle         |
      | ACTIVE    | due     | lines=Desk:4                | 409 DUE_BILLING_PENDING          |
      | ACTIVE    | none    | start_date=2027-02-11        | rejected                        |
      | ACTIVE    | none    | end_date=2027-06-01          | rejected                        |
      | ACTIVE    | none    | payment_terms_days=14        | rejected                        |
